WEBVTT

00:16.960 --> 00:17.800
[pistol clicks]

00:21.920 --> 00:22.800
[thuds]

00:47.760 --> 00:49.280
Arthur took the bullets out.

00:51.040 --> 00:52.360
On the way back.

00:53.400 --> 00:56.360
He said you stopped
at a crossroads to throw up.

01:05.720 --> 01:07.840
You're not even a soldier any more, Tommy.

01:09.280 --> 01:10.800
You didn't check your weapon.

01:12.720 --> 01:14.840
You're not a soldier, you're a coward.

01:15.680 --> 01:17.520
I heard you pull the trigger.

01:18.520 --> 01:20.960
Leaving your family behind
without a goodbye.

01:24.240 --> 01:25.920
If you still need a way out,

01:27.840 --> 01:29.320
here are six of them.

01:45.000 --> 01:47.000
[mud squelching]

02:07.800 --> 02:08.760
[bullets clink]

02:20.360 --> 02:21.200
[sighs]

02:34.000 --> 02:35.080
Mother…

02:38.200 --> 02:39.880
They let you pass through.

02:45.680 --> 02:47.320
They wouldn't let me pass.

02:53.040 --> 02:55.560
As if there were to be
another consequence.

03:05.960 --> 03:07.240
[breathing heavily]

03:12.520 --> 03:13.920
[telephone ringing echoes]

03:21.320 --> 03:23.080
[telephone ringing]

03:49.120 --> 03:49.960
Hello.

03:50.040 --> 03:51.960
[Laura] Mr Shelby,
I imagine you are curious

03:52.040 --> 03:55.080
as to who it was who prevented
the assassination last night.

03:56.120 --> 03:59.320
If you look out your window,
you'll see a flag of truce.

04:00.320 --> 04:01.720
It's a unit of volunteers

04:01.800 --> 04:06.320
bringing the bodies of your dead to you
to send to heaven in your own way.

04:08.680 --> 04:10.960
Last night's operation
was carried out by soldiers

04:11.040 --> 04:13.960
from three Dublin brigades
of the Irish Republican Army.

04:19.400 --> 04:21.800
We need to keep Mr Mosley alive.

04:22.840 --> 04:24.240
That's all you need to know.

04:29.280 --> 04:31.680
Also, you should know
that saving Mosley's life

04:31.760 --> 04:34.040
wasn't our only intervention last night.

04:37.800 --> 04:40.880
We've made some changes
to the structure of your organisation.

04:50.840 --> 04:51.680
[sawing rope]

04:54.960 --> 04:55.800
[sighs]

05:05.160 --> 05:08.720
Ever since you began to build your empire,

05:10.280 --> 05:12.120
you've had a crutch to lean on.

05:15.080 --> 05:17.000
Last night we kicked away that crutch.

05:18.480 --> 05:21.080
From now on,
it will be us that you lean on.

05:22.720 --> 05:26.040
Please be aware, Mr Shelby,
that the deaths of your people

05:27.320 --> 05:29.480
are your own responsibility,

05:30.560 --> 05:35.160
because you consistently fail
to understand your own limitations.

05:36.000 --> 05:36.960
[phone slams]

05:40.600 --> 05:41.480
[knife slashes]

05:54.840 --> 05:55.720
[sighs]

06:10.800 --> 06:12.120
[sobs softly]

06:19.360 --> 06:20.240
[inhales deeply]

06:53.200 --> 06:54.480
[music box playing]

07:04.480 --> 07:05.440
[fire crackling]

07:20.480 --> 07:21.600
[crackling continues]

08:09.840 --> 08:10.760
Mum…

08:14.240 --> 08:17.440
It was the ambitions and strategies
of one man that caused this.

08:21.520 --> 08:23.600
I swear in the name of Almighty God,

08:25.120 --> 08:29.040
no matter what it takes,
no matter how many lies I have to tell…

08:32.760 --> 08:34.800
…I will take revenge on Tommy Shelby.

10:54.480 --> 10:57.880
Sir.

11:00.280 --> 11:02.360
[in French] The island of Miquelon.

11:30.360 --> 11:34.160
[Tommy in French] The commissioner said
to give us two hours. Someone may die.

11:34.680 --> 11:37.200
If it's me, tell them to call my brother.

13:10.720 --> 13:11.560
[bell rings]

13:14.840 --> 13:16.440
[barman in French] I'm coming.

13:16.520 --> 13:17.640
[bottles rattling]

13:31.800 --> 13:35.160
My name is Thomas Shelby.
I have the meeting room booked.

13:35.720 --> 13:36.560
Uh…

13:37.160 --> 13:39.560
Last night, some drunks broke my windows.

13:40.160 --> 13:43.480
Pigeons got inside the big room.
My wife is clearing them out.

13:44.920 --> 13:46.720
I'm early. I'll wait.

13:49.520 --> 13:51.040
[in English] You want a drink?

13:53.840 --> 13:55.720
I'll have a glass of water, please.

14:13.720 --> 14:18.160
Windows got broke because
a lot of people here are drunk and angry.

14:20.440 --> 14:21.360
You know…

14:22.400 --> 14:25.920
Half the men on this island
made their living bootlegging until today.

14:26.840 --> 14:28.880
The other half fixed their boats.

14:33.440 --> 14:35.440
Maybe you should
take your water into the hall.

14:37.480 --> 14:38.320
[clicks tongue]

14:47.520 --> 14:49.440
[in French] Another bottle of whiskey.

14:57.840 --> 14:59.640
You work for the whiskey company, right?

15:13.320 --> 15:15.480
I'm here on private business.

15:21.680 --> 15:23.360
Where did you learn French?

15:23.440 --> 15:24.720
[Tommy] In France.

15:28.000 --> 15:30.720
[in English] Yeah,
I learned a lot of things in France.

15:36.360 --> 15:39.840
Island is crawling
with you fucking commissary men.

15:43.440 --> 15:45.320
Closing our warehouses down.

15:47.680 --> 15:49.320
Throwing men out of work.

15:49.400 --> 15:51.480
[in French]
Jean-Claude, leave the man alone.

15:55.640 --> 15:57.880
[in English] Ten years
our boat ran whiskey,

15:57.960 --> 16:00.040
down the President Roads to Boston.

16:01.440 --> 16:03.560
-Now we have fucking nothing.
-[cork thuds]

16:07.040 --> 16:09.560
And you sit in front of us
and order fucking water.

16:10.760 --> 16:12.120
Is that meant to be a joke?

16:12.920 --> 16:13.840
No.

16:15.520 --> 16:18.920
I ordered water
because I no longer drink alcohol

16:19.960 --> 16:21.000
of any kind.

16:22.000 --> 16:24.360
[in French] Jean-Claude, please.
Leave it alone.

16:25.760 --> 16:27.360
[in English] You, my friend,

16:28.920 --> 16:30.920
are going to drink a toast.

16:31.000 --> 16:34.720
You will raise your glass
to the poor people of Miquelon

16:34.800 --> 16:37.400
whose lives you bastards have destroyed.

16:38.480 --> 16:39.400
Drink it.

16:39.960 --> 16:40.880
Hey…

16:43.120 --> 16:44.040
Drink.

16:46.600 --> 16:48.320
You're not leaving this bar

16:48.400 --> 16:51.200
until you have raised a toast
to the people of Miquelon.

16:54.960 --> 16:55.800
Okay.

16:57.560 --> 16:59.040
[Jean-Claude gulps]

16:59.120 --> 17:00.080
[Tommy] Okay.

17:03.200 --> 17:04.080
[inhales]

17:04.600 --> 17:09.040
I understand that today,
of all days, you would be angry.

17:11.440 --> 17:14.160
But if you had read my card
instead of burning it,

17:14.240 --> 17:17.600
you would realise
that this is a misunderstanding.

17:18.680 --> 17:21.840
Now, I've been very patient,
given the circumstances,

17:22.400 --> 17:23.640
but you need to sit down

17:24.400 --> 17:26.000
and let me read my newspaper.

17:26.080 --> 17:27.000
[scoffs]

17:31.680 --> 17:34.160
[Jean-Claude in French]
He's a good one, isn't he?

17:38.040 --> 17:39.040
[both grunting]

17:41.320 --> 17:44.160
[Tommy in English] Before this goes
any further, let me explain.

17:44.240 --> 17:47.840
I will not drink your toast
because four years ago I forswore alcohol.

17:47.920 --> 17:48.840
[in French] Fuck!

17:50.960 --> 17:54.200
[in English] No. Don't.

17:54.920 --> 17:56.160
[gunshot fires]

17:57.280 --> 18:01.400
Since I forswore alcohol, I've become
a calmer and more peaceful person.

18:02.240 --> 18:03.840
[in French] What happened?

18:06.480 --> 18:07.400
[in English] Get in.

18:08.440 --> 18:09.280
[sighs]

18:12.840 --> 18:16.560
Sometimes, in moments
of personal conflict,

18:17.960 --> 18:20.320
I can resort to my old ways.

18:20.960 --> 18:23.120
If this were to happen now,
it would indeed

18:23.800 --> 18:25.440
be a black day in Miquelon.

18:27.360 --> 18:29.800
Now, my guests will be arriving shortly.

18:29.880 --> 18:31.680
I need to prepare the room.

18:31.760 --> 18:32.920
Can you show me where?

18:39.920 --> 18:41.320
[telephone thuds and rings]

18:44.280 --> 18:46.880
[Michael in French] Excuse me,
where is the Hotel Robert?

18:47.680 --> 18:48.520
[spits]

18:51.080 --> 18:53.160
[Connor in English] They think
we're distillery men

18:53.240 --> 18:54.760
here to take our whiskey back.

18:55.360 --> 18:56.320
We're late.

18:56.400 --> 18:58.160
He's always early. Let's go.

18:58.240 --> 18:59.320
[indistinct chatter]

19:24.320 --> 19:25.200
[exhales]

19:31.840 --> 19:32.720
[sighs]

19:50.040 --> 19:50.880
[door opening]

19:57.560 --> 20:00.480
[Polly] There will be a war
and one of you will die.

20:01.080 --> 20:02.960
But which one, I cannot tell.

20:03.760 --> 20:05.080
[footsteps approaching]

20:22.040 --> 20:23.160
Hello, Tommy.

20:25.040 --> 20:27.480
There's a man out there
having his face stitched back up.

20:27.560 --> 20:30.320
That was a misunderstanding.
Hello, Michael.

20:36.280 --> 20:38.440
I wasn't sure what I'd think
when I saw you again, Tom.

20:38.520 --> 20:41.480
Oh, yeah? What do you think?

20:43.560 --> 20:45.600
Since my mother
passed away four years ago,

20:45.680 --> 20:47.160
Tommy and I haven't even spoken.

20:48.440 --> 20:50.560
[Tommy] Well, we've both been very busy.

20:51.120 --> 20:53.920
You've been too busy
to punish the people who killed her.

20:54.000 --> 20:57.280
You know, Michael, when you're dealing
with a very powerful enemy,

20:58.040 --> 21:00.200
taking revenge sometimes requires time.

21:01.360 --> 21:04.320
You have to pick your moment.

21:05.800 --> 21:06.920
That moment will come.

21:14.120 --> 21:16.400
But now we have
a business interest in common.

21:17.280 --> 21:21.600
And any bad blood will be diluted
by time and a practical self-interest.

21:24.160 --> 21:27.360
Well, Tommy, we're all keen
to hear what you have to say.

21:27.440 --> 21:30.960
I'm looking forward to working with
you again, Michael. You look very well.

21:31.800 --> 21:32.720
You too.

21:33.880 --> 21:34.960
How is the family?

21:35.720 --> 21:36.800
[children chattering]

21:47.840 --> 21:53.080
This projector is a gift
from Charlie-fucking-Chaplin.

21:53.160 --> 21:56.960
And he sent it all the way from Hollywood.
Now sit down and watch the film!

21:57.040 --> 22:00.640
Oh, God. No, Elizabeth, don't do that.
You're gonna hurt yourself.

22:00.720 --> 22:03.120
Yes, hi. Is that the Bell Tavern?

22:03.200 --> 22:05.360
If there's a Gypsy in there
called Johnny Dogs,

22:05.440 --> 22:08.400
can you tell him to come
and round up his fucking kids?

22:08.480 --> 22:10.680
It's Christmas. A time for family.

22:10.760 --> 22:11.880
[receiver thuds]

22:16.280 --> 22:18.440
Mum, I was watching that.

22:20.080 --> 22:22.280
Okay, everyone. Okay.

22:23.520 --> 22:24.680
[girl] When's he coming?

22:24.760 --> 22:27.600
We're having this Christmas party early

22:27.680 --> 22:32.560
because tomorrow, me and Charles and Ruby
are going on a big ship to Canada.

22:32.640 --> 22:34.560
-[boy whispers] Canada.
-To be with their daddy.

22:35.280 --> 22:37.920
But we told
Father Christmas about the party

22:38.840 --> 22:40.520
and he brought you all presents.

22:40.600 --> 22:41.720
[children] Yes!

22:41.800 --> 22:42.680
[Ada laughs]

22:43.640 --> 22:44.640
[boy] Race you!

22:44.720 --> 22:46.800
Ada, where the fuck is Father Christmas?

22:46.880 --> 22:49.800
I don't know.
He was supposed to be here by now.

22:49.880 --> 22:52.360
-Yeah.
-Where the fuck are you, Santa?

22:57.240 --> 22:58.240
[imitates gunshots]

22:59.240 --> 23:00.240
[imitates gasping]

23:01.680 --> 23:02.680
[exclaims]

23:05.280 --> 23:06.640
You've got me.

23:07.800 --> 23:10.280
But I've got a gun. You better run!

23:11.640 --> 23:13.440
You'd better run!

23:14.320 --> 23:16.840
[Tommy] Gentlemen, today is
the last day of Prohibition.

23:17.640 --> 23:19.600
But rather than see it
as the end of something,

23:19.680 --> 23:22.280
I believe that,
for men like us, it can present

23:23.160 --> 23:25.880
a new beginning, a new opportunity.

23:26.520 --> 23:29.880
An opportunity I would like to share
with people I know I can trust.

23:30.960 --> 23:34.040
For the last twelve years,
the men of this island

23:34.600 --> 23:37.600
have been making their living
from bootlegging whiskey,

23:37.680 --> 23:41.480
from navigating the waters
and avoiding American border patrols.

23:41.560 --> 23:44.680
But now that whiskey
is about to become legal,

23:44.760 --> 23:49.000
the trade will fall back into the hands
of capitalists from New York,

23:49.080 --> 23:50.840
Boston and Toronto.

23:50.920 --> 23:51.760
But…

23:53.640 --> 23:55.040
when one door closes…

23:57.520 --> 23:59.280
…another one opens.

23:59.360 --> 24:03.000
We can take advantage of the systems
that are in place on Miquelon Island

24:03.080 --> 24:06.360
and offer selected boat crews
the opportunity to carry on working.

24:06.440 --> 24:09.320
But this time with a different cargo.

24:24.360 --> 24:27.160
-You want me to pour?
-No.

24:34.280 --> 24:36.520
Now it's all over the fucking island.

24:36.600 --> 24:39.040
This is an island
with no morals and no opinions.

24:39.120 --> 24:42.440
Just a load of fucking boats
with nothing to carry and nowhere to go

24:43.680 --> 24:46.400
Reason why Miquelon was used
to run whiskey in the first place

24:46.480 --> 24:49.800
is 'cause it sits outside
the territorial waters of both America

24:50.400 --> 24:51.840
and Canada.

24:51.920 --> 24:53.960
Technically, it's French territory.

24:54.520 --> 24:57.080
The FBI, the RCMP have no jurisdiction.

25:00.080 --> 25:01.720
Where do you get this stuff?

25:02.320 --> 25:04.000
I've established a supply chain

25:04.080 --> 25:06.760
over the last four years
with associates in Belfast.

25:07.920 --> 25:10.800
We decided it was time
to break into the American market.

25:11.360 --> 25:15.160
That, my friend,
is the finest opium in the world.

25:16.440 --> 25:19.640
Delivered to my warehouse
in Liverpool directly from Shanghai.

25:21.640 --> 25:25.640
Michael, when it comes to this shit,
you're the expert.

25:26.160 --> 25:27.080
I trust him.

25:28.280 --> 25:30.120
What about the French police?

25:30.200 --> 25:33.640
I've been in communication
with the Miquelon Prefect de Gendarme.

25:33.720 --> 25:36.040
We fought in
two of the same battles in France.

25:37.360 --> 25:39.160
We consider each other comrades.

25:39.800 --> 25:42.760
I have offered my comrade
twelve million francs

25:42.840 --> 25:45.800
if the boats between
Miquelon and Boston keep running.

25:46.440 --> 25:51.080
We will have to take your proposal
to Uncle Jack in Boston.

25:51.880 --> 25:54.840
Perhaps we can meet after
you've spoken with Uncle Jack, Michael.

25:54.920 --> 25:56.840
Who I believe is your wife's uncle?

25:56.920 --> 25:59.160
-Jack Nelson.
-[Connor] Hey! [chuckles]

26:00.840 --> 26:03.400
The guy knows things
that can get him killed,

26:04.000 --> 26:05.440
and he says them out loud.

26:06.520 --> 26:08.160
I have a high regard for Mr Nelson.

26:09.440 --> 26:11.320
He has a history not unlike my own.

26:11.400 --> 26:13.520
Jack Nelson's past is forgotten.

26:13.600 --> 26:14.880
[Connor] Not forgotten.

26:14.960 --> 26:16.200
Fucking gone.

26:16.280 --> 26:17.200
[Tommy] No, not gone.

26:17.280 --> 26:19.680
Just erased from the records like my own.

26:21.120 --> 26:22.920
Give him my regards, will you?

26:31.720 --> 26:33.560
You haven't touched your drink, Tom.

26:38.880 --> 26:40.840
You know, since we last met, Michael…

26:43.080 --> 26:44.680
Well, I've become a better man.

26:46.600 --> 26:50.480
I now realise that whiskey is just fuel
for the loud engines inside your head.

26:50.560 --> 26:51.880
[men laughing]

26:51.960 --> 26:53.320
Catch yourself on.

26:56.600 --> 26:59.360
What is this guy, a fucking poet? Huh?

26:59.440 --> 27:02.400
Oh, I do read poetry,
but I don't yet write it.

27:05.440 --> 27:07.480
They say the fog is going to get worse.

27:08.200 --> 27:10.720
Better get off this island
before it traps us here.

27:13.120 --> 27:17.720
Just understand,
Uncle Jack decides everything. Okay?

27:18.640 --> 27:21.120
And I decide when the meeting is over.

27:22.000 --> 27:23.440
So sit down till I say.

27:30.920 --> 27:31.840
[scoffs]

27:34.400 --> 27:35.400
[clears throat]

27:42.800 --> 27:43.760
[liquid pours]

27:44.360 --> 27:45.600
[in Irish] Good man.

27:50.440 --> 27:52.600
[in English] Put some fucking hair
on your chest? Huh?

28:00.240 --> 28:01.280
Good boy.

28:01.360 --> 28:02.240
[men chuckle]

28:05.000 --> 28:08.880
Now, give us all a poem before we go.

28:11.680 --> 28:17.120
Want to hear a poem? Want to hear a poem?

28:20.240 --> 28:21.440
What about you?

28:22.400 --> 28:23.520
Brainbox?

28:33.440 --> 28:34.440
[sighs]

28:37.240 --> 28:39.080
I was angry with my friend

28:39.640 --> 28:42.920
I told my wrath, my wrath did end

28:46.360 --> 28:47.880
I was angry with my foe

28:49.320 --> 28:50.400
I told it not

28:52.840 --> 28:54.000
My wrath did grow

29:04.160 --> 29:05.760
It's from The Poison Tree

29:06.720 --> 29:08.720
by William Blake.
You won't have heard of him.

29:11.600 --> 29:12.560
Meeting over.

29:13.960 --> 29:15.200
Oh, and by the way,

29:16.240 --> 29:18.320
my friend, the police commissioner,

29:18.400 --> 29:22.520
told me that he'd spoken
to his FBI liaison officer,

29:23.440 --> 29:28.720
and he told him that there is an informant
in your organisation in South Boston.

29:29.400 --> 29:33.160
I tell you this
in the spirit of corporate hygiene.

29:34.080 --> 29:35.400
Here you are, Michael.

29:40.440 --> 29:43.880
Beware the man
with a bleeding-heart tattoo

29:44.840 --> 29:46.800
with "Maria" written in red.

29:50.600 --> 29:52.120
Have a good day, gentlemen.

29:55.320 --> 29:56.400
[man] Don't bother.

30:15.760 --> 30:17.440
This time, don't burn it.

30:22.600 --> 30:25.200
[in French] Every catastrophe
is also an opportunity.

30:42.440 --> 30:43.400
[Ada] Arthur.

30:49.960 --> 30:50.840
[clicks tongue]

30:53.920 --> 30:55.120
Come on. Come on.

30:55.680 --> 30:56.720
God.

30:57.760 --> 31:01.120
God. If Polly was still here,
she'd never have let it get this bad.

31:01.200 --> 31:02.120
Come on.

31:02.640 --> 31:03.920
Come on, Arthur.

31:04.000 --> 31:04.920
Arthur!

31:05.960 --> 31:08.640
I'm not Polly,
but I am still your fucking sister.

31:09.280 --> 31:11.480
You swore to me you would stop using.

31:12.160 --> 31:13.040
[Arthur sniffs]

31:13.120 --> 31:16.000
It's Christmas Day, Ada. Christmas Day.

31:16.080 --> 31:17.800
Yes, it's Christmas.

31:17.880 --> 31:20.000
So where the fuck
are the fucking presents?

31:20.960 --> 31:22.520
I'll be all right in a bit…

31:23.360 --> 31:24.320
[Ada sighs]

31:25.240 --> 31:26.160
Great.

31:26.800 --> 31:28.840
My brother off his face on junk.

31:28.920 --> 31:29.960
[Arthur groans]

31:30.040 --> 31:32.360
Every day is a question without an answer.

31:34.160 --> 31:35.680
A leak without a bucket.

31:37.160 --> 31:38.760
Me without a clue what to do.

31:42.120 --> 31:42.960
Fuck!

31:45.800 --> 31:47.000
[Arthur] I love you, Ada.

31:48.960 --> 31:50.280
[children chattering]

31:52.520 --> 31:54.680
[man] Children, Father Christmas has been.

31:54.760 --> 31:56.200
[children] Father Christmas!

31:57.880 --> 31:58.920
[boy] Go. Go on.

31:59.000 --> 32:00.440
[girl] What did you ask for?

32:01.160 --> 32:02.320
[man] What have we got?

32:02.840 --> 32:05.600
Father Christmas got
stuck up the chimney again, did he?

32:05.680 --> 32:06.520
[Ada] Mmm.

32:07.240 --> 32:08.840
What ship are you on tomorrow?

32:09.440 --> 32:10.280
[sighs]

32:10.360 --> 32:13.160
Oh, the best, most expensive one.

32:14.280 --> 32:17.040
And then we'll get there.
And Tommy will say,

32:17.120 --> 32:19.840
"Hello, Lizzie. Hello, children."

32:19.920 --> 32:21.000
In that dead voice.

32:21.960 --> 32:23.320
Come on, Lizzie.

32:23.400 --> 32:24.760
He'll be on holiday.

32:24.840 --> 32:26.320
Being away might change him.

32:28.240 --> 32:29.680
Even on holiday, Ada.

32:30.720 --> 32:32.080
Even on top of a rocky mountain,

32:32.160 --> 32:34.600
he'll be the same way
he's been since Polly died.

32:35.840 --> 32:40.880
No more Polly,
no more whiskey, no more Tommy.

32:53.160 --> 32:54.080
[Tommy sighs]

32:57.640 --> 32:59.440
[bird chirping]

33:02.240 --> 33:04.240
[in French] Put me through
to Detective Lawrence

33:04.320 --> 33:06.000
at St John's Harbour Marine Police.

33:09.880 --> 33:13.520
[in English] Yeah, I'm calling from
Miquelon Island. From the police station.

33:14.000 --> 33:17.280
There is a boat leaving the island
now, heading across the border.

33:18.040 --> 33:20.040
When it docks at St John's,

33:20.600 --> 33:23.920
a man named Michael Gray
will board a ferry to Boston.

33:24.480 --> 33:25.680
Listen very carefully.

33:26.320 --> 33:31.520
He's wearing a dark coat, a blue suit
and carrying a black briefcase.

33:31.600 --> 33:36.200
Inside the briefcase
is five pound of pure, refined opium.

33:37.680 --> 33:39.160
A concerned citizen.

33:40.240 --> 33:41.800
Yeah, my name is Mr Jones.

33:42.680 --> 33:43.560
[receiver thuds]

33:45.360 --> 33:46.440
[sighs]

33:49.600 --> 33:51.440
[commissioner in French] You want a drink?

33:51.520 --> 33:53.400
-[rubs hands]
-[in English] Yes, I do.

33:55.040 --> 33:56.400
But I don't drink any more.

33:58.840 --> 34:00.040
[commissioner in French] Why?

34:01.400 --> 34:02.320
[Tommy sighs]

34:06.600 --> 34:07.840
I have business.

34:09.400 --> 34:11.040
I need to get off this island.

34:12.080 --> 34:13.000
[telephone rings]

34:15.000 --> 34:16.560
[Ada] You shouldn't be in here, Karl.

34:17.360 --> 34:18.600
[telephone ringing]

34:26.840 --> 34:28.080
Are you gonna answer it?

34:28.680 --> 34:30.440
No, I don't work for him any more.

34:35.800 --> 34:37.000
It might be important.

34:37.080 --> 34:38.960
[Ada] That's why
I don't want to answer it.

34:39.040 --> 34:40.000
[ringing continues]

34:42.200 --> 34:43.680
-Can I answer it?
-No.

34:50.640 --> 34:51.480
[Ada sighs]

34:52.760 --> 34:53.680
Hello.

34:54.640 --> 34:55.480
Mmm-hmm.

34:57.000 --> 34:57.920
Fuck!

34:58.640 --> 34:59.720
[indistinct chattering]

35:31.800 --> 35:33.520
Do you know who this man is?

35:35.840 --> 35:36.720
[sighs]

35:47.280 --> 35:49.600
All right. Come on, Arthur.

35:54.680 --> 35:55.760
Ada…

35:59.360 --> 36:00.960
[Arthur groans]

36:02.280 --> 36:03.800
Hey, that tickles.

36:10.000 --> 36:14.480
His brother, Thomas Shelby,
says don't serve him opium ever again.

36:15.120 --> 36:19.280
Or someone will write Arthur Shelby's name
on your chest with a bayonet.

37:10.600 --> 37:12.760
So… What the fuck?

37:12.840 --> 37:14.680
I can't talk about anything in here.

37:15.560 --> 37:18.240
I just wanted to see your face
and smell your perfume.

37:18.720 --> 37:22.240
Tommy Shelby steps back into your life
and right away, this is what happens?

37:22.320 --> 37:24.360
-No names in here.
-Sorry.

37:25.400 --> 37:28.200
-Let's just call him the Devil.
-Take a seat.

37:31.120 --> 37:32.280
[sighs] How is Laurence?

37:32.960 --> 37:36.080
Oh, you know, missing his father.

37:36.680 --> 37:38.560
What the fuck happened, Michael?

37:39.720 --> 37:41.560
-It's in hand.
-Whose hand?

37:43.040 --> 37:44.440
No, really.

37:44.520 --> 37:46.720
Whose fucking hand, Michael?

37:46.800 --> 37:47.680
Huh?

37:55.400 --> 37:58.920
Like everything else in this city,
it's in the hand of your Uncle Jack.

37:59.440 --> 38:02.000
I need him to get the charges lifted
and get me out of here.

38:02.080 --> 38:03.560
I already talked to him.

38:04.240 --> 38:06.160
He told me what the Devil proposed.

38:07.480 --> 38:10.360
Tommy Shelby wants
to do business with Jack Nelson?

38:11.080 --> 38:13.000
He wants to take on Boston?

38:13.080 --> 38:14.440
No one is taking on anyone.

38:15.200 --> 38:19.000
It's in hand. There are deals
being made at a high level,

38:19.080 --> 38:22.560
but there are some people at the middle
and lower levels who cannot be trusted.

38:22.640 --> 38:25.200
-Michael, this sounds fucking--
-Shut up and listen.

38:27.120 --> 38:29.800
It was Tommy himself
who warned us of the informant.

38:30.800 --> 38:33.640
We're guessing that the informant
tipped off the police about me.

38:35.520 --> 38:37.600
Then the Devil's plan has already begun.

38:38.400 --> 38:41.320
What's the point of ships and planes
if you can't get away?

38:41.800 --> 38:44.840
Gina, in today's paper,
you'll read about a man

38:44.920 --> 38:47.720
being fished out of the Boston Harbour
with a bleeding-heart tattoo

38:47.800 --> 38:49.560
and the name "Maria" written on his arm.

38:49.640 --> 38:51.280
Single shot to the head.

38:51.360 --> 38:53.320
Yeah, I know. I read it already.

38:55.400 --> 38:57.000
His death will lead to others.

38:58.320 --> 39:01.920
For this business to work,
we must only use men we trust.

39:02.480 --> 39:04.600
And while the clean-up
is being carried out,

39:05.200 --> 39:06.880
you must keep things to yourself.

39:07.680 --> 39:10.520
You talk loose to anyone,
it'll be me in the harbour

39:10.600 --> 39:13.640
and you'll be the Maria
with the bleeding heart. Understand?

39:19.280 --> 39:20.920
Michael, I just want the truth.

39:23.840 --> 39:27.080
No, fuck that. I need the truth.
Why are you doing business with him again?

39:27.160 --> 39:31.400
Gina, tell me what you're thinking
of getting Laurence for Christmas.

39:31.480 --> 39:34.640
There are plenty of men
who can supply powder all over the world.

39:34.720 --> 39:36.880
I don't understand why it needs to be him.

39:37.960 --> 39:39.320
[Michael sighs]

39:45.680 --> 39:48.480
Some of my business
with Tommy Shelby is unfinished.

39:49.600 --> 39:51.760
This is my opportunity to finish it.

39:55.680 --> 39:58.400
So speak to your uncle
and get me the fuck out of here.

39:59.360 --> 40:00.760
[upbeat music playing]

40:13.560 --> 40:14.800
[telephone ringing]

40:19.080 --> 40:20.000
Hello?

40:21.040 --> 40:21.880
Who?

40:24.240 --> 40:25.080
Sure.

40:26.160 --> 40:27.280
Why the hell not?

40:34.480 --> 40:35.720
[chuckling]

40:39.120 --> 40:40.080
[music continues]

40:45.080 --> 40:48.760
I heard you were in town,
and I thought, "Well, hey…"

40:51.240 --> 40:52.960
"Little man hitting the big time."

40:53.880 --> 40:55.640
-You like jazz?
-[Tommy] No.

40:57.200 --> 40:58.400
[jazz music plays louder]

41:00.600 --> 41:01.760
[music stops]

41:01.840 --> 41:03.520
What do you want, whiskey?

41:03.600 --> 41:04.800
Water.

41:04.880 --> 41:07.160
I don't have any water.
What else do you want?

41:08.120 --> 41:11.880
I have a message for your Uncle Jack.

41:11.960 --> 41:13.720
[Gina] Tommy, relax.

41:16.400 --> 41:17.520
Have a fucking drink.

41:19.360 --> 41:22.480
You know, my uncle is planning on buying
the United States import licence

41:22.560 --> 41:25.680
to all the best Scotch
and Irish whiskey distilleries?

41:27.280 --> 41:28.120
[glass thuds]

41:28.200 --> 41:30.800
He's on his way to London
right now to make those deals.

41:30.880 --> 41:34.520
Every drop in every state
will be another dime for Uncle Jack.

41:35.320 --> 41:39.160
Yep. He's a very powerful,
very impressive man.

41:40.200 --> 41:42.680
I've only seen photographs
when he was young.

41:42.760 --> 41:43.960
Police mug shots.

41:44.520 --> 41:46.920
And more recently
in high society magazines.

41:47.640 --> 41:49.680
I think this represents progress.

41:50.320 --> 41:51.240
[Gina] Yeah.

41:53.000 --> 41:55.600
And before you tell me
what you want me to tell him,

41:56.240 --> 41:58.080
I have a message from him to you.

41:59.880 --> 42:00.840
No deal.

42:04.720 --> 42:05.960
Hmm.

42:07.840 --> 42:12.000
In England, when someone gets this close
to Tommy Shelby, it's, "Oh, the horror."

42:14.600 --> 42:16.000
"Oh, the desire."

42:17.240 --> 42:21.560
To fall on your knees,
open your mouth and say, "Yes, sir."

42:22.960 --> 42:24.360
"Please, sir."

42:28.640 --> 42:31.240
So it's Uncle Jack
you fall on your knees for, eh?

42:32.360 --> 42:33.440
Not Michael?

42:35.640 --> 42:38.080
He says no deal, Mr Shelby.

42:41.480 --> 42:43.440
You smell of jail, Gina.

42:44.200 --> 42:46.000
-And you drink too much.
-[chuckles]

42:47.400 --> 42:49.040
Yes, but booze is legal.

42:50.440 --> 42:51.760
Your white powder is not.

42:53.120 --> 42:57.080
Jack has friends in the government now.
You have any idea of how far he's risen?

42:58.880 --> 43:01.720
All the way to the fucking top.

43:03.520 --> 43:05.680
Can't have white powder
on his shiny, black boots

43:05.760 --> 43:08.400
when he's meeting
the president of the United States.

43:08.480 --> 43:11.920
'Cause, yeah, that's where he goes now.

43:13.760 --> 43:17.480
So he can't really be taking
such a big risk on such a little deal.

43:19.520 --> 43:21.320
Go home, boy.

43:24.160 --> 43:25.480
Bye-bye, Mr Shelby.

43:28.160 --> 43:31.440
Yeah, you have another whiskey, Gina.
Another dime for Uncle Jack.

43:32.280 --> 43:33.400
You mind if I smoke?

43:34.040 --> 43:35.600
If it's legal, it's okay.

43:37.880 --> 43:39.360
Before I go,

43:40.760 --> 43:41.800
you should know…

43:44.560 --> 43:45.400
that it was me

43:46.280 --> 43:51.000
who tipped off the border police
about the contents of Michael's suitcase.

43:54.000 --> 43:55.440
I'm the reason he's in jail.

43:59.400 --> 44:01.520
I wanted to give your uncle a dilemma.

44:03.880 --> 44:06.040
His favourite niece's husband

44:07.120 --> 44:11.120
banged up in Boston for smuggling opium.

44:13.200 --> 44:14.120
What does he do?

44:15.600 --> 44:18.600
If he intervenes, has him released,
how'll that play in the Oval Office?

44:18.680 --> 44:20.120
If he does nothing,

44:21.240 --> 44:22.800
how does that play in South Boston?

44:22.880 --> 44:23.920
Oh, fuck you.

44:28.720 --> 44:29.640
Fine.

44:30.560 --> 44:31.520
Stay here.

44:33.000 --> 44:35.840
Deal here, die here,
for all I fucking care.

44:35.920 --> 44:36.880
[music starts]

44:41.160 --> 44:42.680
Die at whose hand, Gina?

44:43.760 --> 44:44.880
[music stops abruptly]

44:46.720 --> 44:48.960
My message to your uncle is this.

44:51.000 --> 44:55.480
If he doesn't want to buy my opium,
I will sell to the East Boston Jews.

45:01.920 --> 45:02.920
[Gina] Oh, baby.

45:04.520 --> 45:06.920
Do you want to start a fucking war?

45:07.440 --> 45:09.040
With that amount of opium,

45:10.160 --> 45:11.360
the balance of power

45:12.080 --> 45:15.840
between the Irish,
the Jewish and the Italians

45:17.040 --> 45:19.120
would shift heavily in favour of the East.

45:21.120 --> 45:25.320
I have excellent contacts
with the family that runs East Boston.

45:25.960 --> 45:28.880
The Solomons family.
Maybe you've heard of 'em?

45:31.120 --> 45:35.920
Once you people have accepted
that you must treat us as equals…

45:39.680 --> 45:42.520
then I think our families
will work together very well.

45:45.200 --> 45:46.600
Have a good day, Gina.

45:52.080 --> 45:53.760
[kicks speaker and music resumes]

46:04.400 --> 46:05.560
[telephone ringing]

46:07.800 --> 46:09.200
[sighs] Yep?

46:11.360 --> 46:13.080
Yes, I'll accept the call.

46:23.160 --> 46:24.240
[Tommy] Hello, Lizzie.

46:24.960 --> 46:25.960
Tommy…

46:27.800 --> 46:29.320
It's Ruby, she's not well.

46:31.040 --> 46:32.800
She's got a temperature of 101.

46:32.880 --> 46:34.000
Doctor's just left.

46:35.000 --> 46:36.080
What did he say?

46:36.160 --> 46:37.680
He says he thinks it's flu.

46:37.760 --> 46:40.400
But he's gonna come later to check on her.

46:42.320 --> 46:43.640
She's been coughing, and…

46:46.360 --> 46:47.440
[sighs]

46:47.520 --> 46:51.680
Tommy, he said it's…
not a good idea for us to travel.

46:53.120 --> 46:55.480
We can't board that ship to Boston today.

46:56.400 --> 46:58.320
That's all right, Lizzie, don't worry.

46:59.200 --> 47:02.480
Don't worry, you just stay there
for now and get her better and…

47:03.280 --> 47:05.320
[clears throat] Can I speak to her?

47:05.400 --> 47:06.320
She's sleeping.

47:07.320 --> 47:08.720
Yeah. Well, let her sleep.

47:10.200 --> 47:11.120
Let her sleep.

47:12.600 --> 47:15.000
Lizzie, I've a bit more
business to do here.

47:16.400 --> 47:20.160
Look, you just book a new passage
when Ruby's feeling better.

47:20.240 --> 47:22.960
Doesn't matter if you're not here
for Christmas. Just get here.

47:23.840 --> 47:26.320
And then I'll get this business done.

47:27.920 --> 47:31.240
You get here with the children,
and then no more.

47:32.640 --> 47:36.680
And it'll just be us
and the clean air out in the West.

47:37.280 --> 47:39.320
I found a place in the mountains.

47:39.400 --> 47:40.680
There'll be snow.

47:40.760 --> 47:43.560
Tell Ruby I'll build her a snowman.

47:43.640 --> 47:44.520
[Lizzie chuckles]

47:45.240 --> 47:46.160
[Tommy sighs]

47:46.840 --> 47:48.400
How long has she been coughing?

47:48.960 --> 47:52.760
A few days. She's been out
running wild with Johnny Dogs' kids

47:52.840 --> 47:54.480
out in the cold by the river.

47:56.520 --> 47:57.400
[sighs]

47:59.320 --> 48:00.800
Are you okay, Tommy?

48:01.840 --> 48:03.480
Your voice, it sounds different.

48:04.200 --> 48:05.280
It's just cold.

48:06.400 --> 48:08.320
I'll get this business done in Boston.

48:09.320 --> 48:10.600
That'll be the end of it.

48:12.840 --> 48:14.040
Then I just want to…

48:16.200 --> 48:19.280
I just want to pick Ruby up
and hold her in my arms, you know?

48:20.720 --> 48:22.640
I miss the weight of carrying her.

48:22.720 --> 48:24.280
I gave her her presents early.

48:25.040 --> 48:26.200
She loves them.

48:28.960 --> 48:34.320
Last night she was burning up.
She was delirious. She kept talking.

48:34.400 --> 48:37.120
Johnny's kids have been
teaching her to speak Gypsy.

48:37.200 --> 48:38.040
[chuckles]

48:38.680 --> 48:40.840
Teaching her to rob and steal, more like.

48:40.920 --> 48:41.960
[chuckles] Yeah.

48:44.480 --> 48:47.960
When she was delirious,
she kept saying these Gypsy words…

48:50.360 --> 48:55.720
"Tickner Maura, Tickner Maura,
O Beng, O Beng." Over and over again.

48:57.400 --> 48:58.800
What? Lizzie, what…

49:00.320 --> 49:02.160
What did you say? What did Ruby say?

49:02.800 --> 49:05.480
Tickner. Tickner Maura…
Something like that.

49:05.560 --> 49:08.560
Did she say any other words
that you didn't understand?

49:11.400 --> 49:12.960
O Beng. I don't know--

49:13.040 --> 49:16.640
No, Lizzie, did she say any other words
in Romany? Fucking listen to me.

49:16.720 --> 49:18.840
I don't know Romany words, Tommy.

49:18.920 --> 49:19.800
I don't think so.

49:19.880 --> 49:22.200
Just "Tickner Maura" and "O Beng"?

49:22.280 --> 49:23.160
Yes.

49:23.240 --> 49:25.280
She see anything when she was burning up?

49:25.360 --> 49:26.680
-What could she see?
-Fuck.

49:26.760 --> 49:28.920
Please just answer the fucking question!

49:29.000 --> 49:31.160
She said she could see a man.

49:31.960 --> 49:33.840
A man with green eyes.

49:34.800 --> 49:37.000
She was delirious. She was burning up.

49:37.480 --> 49:39.000
What the fuck is the matter?

49:39.080 --> 49:41.240
All right, listen, Lizzie,
I'm coming home.

49:41.320 --> 49:42.840
It's just a fever, love.

49:42.920 --> 49:44.760
I'm coming home on the next steamer.

49:44.840 --> 49:47.680
You keep her out of school,
and you keep her away from--

49:47.760 --> 49:49.600
-Tommy--
-Keep her away from the river.

49:49.680 --> 49:51.800
Don't let her ride a horse
or go near a horse.

49:51.880 --> 49:55.680
Tell Johnny Dogs and his wives
the words that Ruby has been saying.

49:55.760 --> 49:59.920
Do you hear me? Tell Johnny's eldest wife
to put a Black Madonna around her neck.

50:00.000 --> 50:03.000
You listen to Esmeralda
the same way you listen to a doctor.

50:03.080 --> 50:05.360
-You hear me?
-Fucking Gypsy stuff.

50:05.440 --> 50:09.080
Yes, it is Gypsy fucking stuff, Lizzie!
Yes, it fucking is!

50:09.160 --> 50:10.800
-[scoffs]
-And you get Curly there.

50:10.880 --> 50:13.480
Tell him to stay in the stable
with Ruby's horses.

50:13.560 --> 50:16.480
And you do everything that Johnny Dogs
and his wives fucking tell you.

50:16.560 --> 50:17.720
Do you understand me?

50:19.240 --> 50:21.320
I'm sorry, Lizzie. Do you understand?

50:21.400 --> 50:22.360
Okay.

50:23.560 --> 50:24.720
I'll do it.

50:24.800 --> 50:26.160
All right, I'm coming home.

50:26.880 --> 50:27.720
[receiver bangs]

50:28.280 --> 50:29.160
[sighs]

50:31.280 --> 50:32.280
[sighs]

50:36.800 --> 50:37.760
Polly?

50:40.160 --> 50:41.080
Polly?

50:44.680 --> 50:46.320
They know I'm trying to get out.

50:47.800 --> 50:51.280
Pol, they're coming for me.

50:53.120 --> 50:54.680
[footsteps echo]

51:31.560 --> 51:34.440
-You son of a fucking bitch.
-[Tommy] You sound American, Michael.

51:36.640 --> 51:39.720
I have to go back to England early.
Let's make this quick, eh?

51:39.800 --> 51:43.320
-You just fuck people up and you run away.
-No, this business will continue.

51:43.400 --> 51:45.600
Jack Nelson is also travelling to England.

51:45.680 --> 51:48.960
To London and to Edinburgh
to buy import licences.

51:49.040 --> 51:51.080
How do you know
where Jack Nelson is going?

51:51.160 --> 51:53.040
Well, I have copies of his itinerary.

51:53.600 --> 51:54.960
Of his personal correspondence.

51:55.040 --> 51:58.680
Letters from the president of
the United States and his many mistresses.

51:58.760 --> 52:00.600
I have contacts in his organisation.

52:01.320 --> 52:04.360
An Irishman with a mortgage
is a powerful resource, Michael.

52:06.560 --> 52:07.800
You're dead, Tommy.

52:08.880 --> 52:10.600
You're out of your fucking depth.

52:12.480 --> 52:13.680
You're dead already.

52:16.360 --> 52:18.240
You threatened to sell to the Jews.

52:18.320 --> 52:22.480
I have contacts in this prison. These boys
will look after you during your stay.

52:22.560 --> 52:24.560
I don't need your people to look after me.

52:24.640 --> 52:26.920
-Jack Nelson's getting me out of here.
-[Tommy] Yeah?

52:27.960 --> 52:28.960
Is he?

52:30.080 --> 52:33.080
This is a letter…
Here, give him this letter, will you?

52:33.160 --> 52:35.840
This is a letter
from the president's personal secretary,

52:35.920 --> 52:38.880
suggesting Jack Nelson
keep you in here for a while longer.

52:38.960 --> 52:41.160
Just until the press
lose interest, Michael.

52:44.720 --> 52:45.880
Fuck you.

52:45.960 --> 52:47.720
[Tommy] You'll be released eventually.

52:48.480 --> 52:52.160
And then you can execute
your business with me as before.

52:53.400 --> 52:56.880
Our business being five million dollars
for a shipment of powder.

52:57.480 --> 53:00.120
And when the exchange is done,
we can shake hands

53:00.200 --> 53:02.560
and go our separate ways once more, eh?

53:06.240 --> 53:07.520
So, you didn't learn.

53:09.760 --> 53:12.120
When my mother died
at the hands of your ambition,

53:12.200 --> 53:13.960
you didn't learn your limitations.

53:16.400 --> 53:17.800
I have no limitations.

53:23.600 --> 53:25.200
Oh, and by the way, Michael,

53:26.400 --> 53:29.120
according to
Jack Nelson's personal accounts,

53:29.200 --> 53:33.120
he bought passage for five people
from Boston to Liverpool.

53:33.200 --> 53:36.360
Five people. His wife, his mistress,

53:36.440 --> 53:39.440
President Roosevelt's son, himself,

53:41.360 --> 53:42.640
and Gina Gray.

53:45.080 --> 53:46.760
Gina's coming to London, Michael.

53:47.680 --> 53:49.440
Where I'll be happy
to show her the sights.

53:49.520 --> 53:52.640
Fuck! You fucking bastard, Tommy!

53:52.720 --> 53:55.640
-Spirits, Boston-Irish, Uncle Jack.
-[Michael] You're the Devil!

53:55.720 --> 53:58.080
-The fucking Devil!
-I'm ready for the conversation.
